				preload="metadata"
				class="img-fluid w-100"
				style="min-height: 20vh; max-height: 65vh;"
			><source
						src="/vis/a000000/a003900/a003912/ecco2_sst_flow.webmhd.webm"
						type="video/webm"
					><source
						src="/vis/a000000/a003900/a003912/ecco2_sst_flow.mp4"
						type="video/mp4"
					><source
						src="/vis/a000000/a003900/a003912/flat_global_ecco2_2028x1024_comp_p30.mp4"
						type="video/mp4"
					><source
						src="/vis/a000000/a003900/a003912/ecco2_sst_flow.m4v"
						type="None"
					><source
						src="/vis/a000000/a003900/a003912/Oceanflows-UHD-2160.mp4"
						type="video/mp4"
					><p class="text-white">
					Global sea surface currents colored by temperature.  These are the assembled (contiguous) versions of the animation.  There are several resolutions to choose from, some are cropped for various purposes.  The 6840x3420 version is the complete, full resolution visualization at the appropriate 2x1 aspect ratio and has not been cropped or resized.  The time range for these visualizations is from 2007-03-25T12:00Z to 2008-03-03T12:00Z.
				</p></video></div><div class="p-2 p-md-3 mb-0-last-p clearfix"><div class="hstack gap-2 flex-wrap flex-lg-nowrap float-end"><ul class="hstack list-unstyled ms-auto gap-2 flex-shrink-0 mb-0"><li><button
